# Extracted data is NOT committed by default.
#
# data/ currently holds subsets from two different provenances, and only one of
# them is cleared for redistribution:
#
#   PUBLIC  - derived from the ENWRA/LPSNRD public release (see PROVENANCE.md)
#   PRIVATE - derived from the Workbench exports delivered by Ted Asch,
#             pending his permission
#
# Ignoring the directory means a stray `git add -A` cannot publish the private
# half. Add cleared files deliberately with `git add -f <path>`.
#
# This matters more than usual here: the repo is private now and will be flipped
# public, and flipping publishes the whole history, not just the current tree.
data/
